Kiwi: A Framework for developing graphical applications in Python.

Kiwi is a framework, composed of a set of modules, which eases Python
development using PyGObject and GTK3. Kiwi makes graphical applications
*much* faster to code, with good architecture and bindings that are more
Pythonic; it also offers extended widgets based upon the original GTK+
widgets.

* Requirements

    - Python >= 3.12
    - PyGObject (gi)    https://pygobject.readthedocs.io/
    - GTK+ 3.x          https://gtk.org/

  Optional

    - zope.interface    https://pypi.org/project/zope.interface/

* Installation

    System dependencies (Ubuntu/Debian):

        sudo apt install python3-gi python3-gi-cairo gir1.2-gtk-3.0 \
                         python3-cairo python3-zope.interface

    Install with pip:

        pip install .

    Or install in development mode:

        pip install -e .

    You can also fetch the latest source code from github:

        git clone https://github.com/stoq/kiwi.git

* Contribute

    Development dependencies (Ubuntu/Debian):

        sudo apt install make python3-pytest python3-mock python3-gi

    Run tests:

        make check

* Directory Layout

    bin/

        Scripts which are going to be installed

    examples/

        Contains a number of examples, most of which are referenced in
        the documentation.

    kiwi/

        Contains the module code itself; this is installed into your
        Python's site-packages directory by setup.py.

    doc/

        Contains documentation for Kiwi, including the LaTeX source code
        which can be used to rebuild the docs. doc/Makefile contains
        commands to regenerate the full set of docs.

    extra/

        Helper scripts that can be used to accelerate certain tasks.

    glade/

        Glade files used by kiwi itself

    pixmaps/

        Pixmaps, images etc

    po/

        Translations

    tests/

        Contains a number of test cases for the Kiwi widgets and
        framework. All checkins and additions of new code should be
        preceded by a working testcase.

    tools/

        Useful scripts

* Contact info:

    URL and download: https://github.com/stoq/kiwi

